From 75f84d199a53bb103d104ea2cab16c599daf322b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vladimir Oltean <vladimir.oltean@nxp.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 15:44:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 41/48] net: pcs: mtip_backplane: ignore reserved bits in C72
 update requests

IEEE 802.3 clause 72 maps coefficient updates, INIT and PRESET to
specific bits, but leaves several bits reserved.

In mtip_rx_c72_wait_ack(), the code polls for LT_COEF_UPD_NOTHING (i.e.
val == 0) to verify the Link Partner dropped its request. If the LP
transmits a non-zero reserved bit (which is allowed/ignored by the
standard), this poll will inevitably time out, failing Link Training.

In mtip_rx_c72_coef_update(), if a reserved bit is set,
LT_COEF_UPD_ANYTHING will endlessly trigger true, bombarding the state
machine with bogus requests that get discarded.

Redefine the macros to explicitly mask out reserved bits.

Signed-off-by: Vladimir Oltean <vladimir.oltean@nxp.com>
---
 drivers/net/pcs/mtip_backplane.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/pcs/mtip_backplane.c b/drivers/net/pcs/mtip_backplane.c
index 86452ba1d63a..108953a540b2 100644
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/mtip_backplane.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/mtip_backplane.c
@@ -62,8 +62,10 @@
 					LT_COZ(COEF_UPD_HOLD) | \
 					LT_COP1(COEF_UPD_HOLD))
 
-#define LT_COEF_UPD_ANYTHING(x)		((x) != 0)
-#define LT_COEF_UPD_NOTHING(x)		((x) == 0)
+#define LT_COEF_UPD_VALID_MASK		(LT_COEF_UPD_MASK | LT_COEF_UPD_INIT | \
+					 LT_COEF_UPD_PRESET)
+#define LT_COEF_UPD_ANYTHING(x)		(((x) & LT_COEF_UPD_VALID_MASK) != 0)
+#define LT_COEF_UPD_NOTHING(x)		(((x) & LT_COEF_UPD_VALID_MASK) == 0)
 
 #define LT_COEF_UPD_INIT		BIT(12)
 #define LT_COEF_UPD_PRESET		BIT(13)
